# Recovery training from placed lying starts against a hidden get-up reference on absolute.args; RECOVERY.md defines
# each option and its rows.
# "StableMimic" marks a value taken from StableMimic (arXiv 2608.02385v1); every other value is this repository's choice.
@absolute.args
# StableMimic, Sections III-B and III-D: tracking and recovery starts are drawn equally often.
--recovery-share 0.5
# The get-up recordings of the 40-clip library whose rows are recovery starts and the hidden reference.
--recovery-hidden-clips fallAndGetUp1_subject1 fallAndGetUp1_subject5 fallAndGetUp2_subject2 fallAndGetUp2_subject3
    fallAndGetUp3_subject1
# StableMimic, Section IV-A: no command comes from a get-up recording (its commands come only from the LAFAN1 dance
# subset, disjoint from its get-up library). The list (the six get-up recordings of the library, fallAndGetUp1_subject4
# included) and drawing commands from every other clip are this repository's choice.
--recovery-command-excluded-clips fallAndGetUp1_subject1 fallAndGetUp1_subject4 fallAndGetUp1_subject5
    fallAndGetUp2_subject2 fallAndGetUp2_subject3 fallAndGetUp3_subject1
# A low row: pelvis below 0.50 m, or pelvis up axis tilted beyond 60 degrees (world z below 0.5).
--recovery-low-pelvis 0.50 0.5
# Upright run that ends a get-up: 50 rows (1 s); longest span from a start row to its get-up end: 375 rows (7.5 s);
# upright rows ahead of a command row: 500 (the 10 s episode limit).
--recovery-rows 50 375 500
# StableMimic, Section III-C: the tracking terms of the get-up reference weigh 2.5 times the command's.
--recovery-reward-scale 2.5
# StableMimic, Section III-B: 2.0 s (100 controls) of target error stops a recovery episode, and the transition back to
# the command lasts 1.5 s (75 controls). Counting the error over consecutive controls and the linear weight of the
# transition are this repository's choice; the paper gives neither.
--recovery-controls 100 75
